WEBVTT

00:00:00.286 --> 00:00:04.779
Mia, this plant has never ordered
a pizza, yet it grows new leaves.

00:00:05.138 --> 00:00:06.704
Where does its food come from?

00:00:07.452 --> 00:00:08.159
The soil.

00:00:08.484 --> 00:00:10.873
Roots are tiny straws sucking up dinner.

00:00:11.267 --> 00:00:12.424
Very muddy dinner.

00:00:13.129 --> 00:00:15.254
My imaginary teacher tears are back.

00:00:15.516 --> 00:00:17.972
Roots absorb water and mineral ions.

00:00:18.361 --> 00:00:22.306
A green plant makes its own
food, glucose, by photosynthesis.

00:00:22.692 --> 00:00:25.637
Calling soil its food could
lose the explanation mark.

00:00:26.392 --> 00:00:28.494
So the plant has a kitchen in its leaves.

00:00:29.023 --> 00:00:30.602
Who pays the electricity bill?

00:00:31.383 --> 00:00:32.899
Light supplies the energy.

00:00:33.215 --> 00:00:34.597
Chlorophyll absorbs it.

00:00:35.065 --> 00:00:38.438
Carbon dioxide from the air and
water are the raw materials.

00:00:38.786 --> 00:00:41.971
The plant uses them to build
glucose and releases oxygen.

00:00:42.719 --> 00:00:44.908
Light goes in, food comes out.

00:00:45.315 --> 00:00:46.829
Is it creating energy again?

00:00:47.625 --> 00:00:48.010
No.

00:00:48.563 --> 00:00:52.663
Energy is transferred from light into
chemical energy stored in glucose.

00:00:53.084 --> 00:00:55.600
Atoms are rearranged, not created.

00:00:56.052 --> 00:00:58.922
The kitchen is a useful
picture, but a leaf has chemical

00:00:58.923 --> 00:01:01.031
reactions, not tiny chefs.

00:01:01.799 --> 00:01:05.905
No chefs, no pizza, just
impressive chemistry.

00:01:06.635 --> 00:01:07.362
Exactly.

00:01:07.692 --> 00:01:11.753
Plants are producers because they make
organic food from simple substances.

00:01:12.182 --> 00:01:15.290
Animals get that food by
eating plants or other animals.

00:01:15.739 --> 00:01:18.673
Nearly every food chain
begins with photosynthesis.

00:01:19.468 --> 00:01:23.891
Then my lunch was once connected to
sunlight, even if I ate it indoors.

00:01:24.617 --> 00:01:25.130
Yes.

00:01:25.449 --> 00:01:29.741
Photosynthetic plants, algae
and bacteria also supply oxygen.

00:01:30.421 --> 00:01:34.719
Growing plants take up carbon dioxide
and store some carbon in their bodies.

00:01:35.342 --> 00:01:37.606
Let's follow that carbon
onto our whiteboard

00:01:37.999 --> 00:01:39.782
Build the word equation for me.

00:01:40.271 --> 00:01:42.249
What belongs on the left of the arrow?

00:01:43.025 --> 00:01:47.691
Carbon dioxide and water, the
raw materials or reactants.

00:01:48.511 --> 00:01:51.396
And the products on the right?

00:01:52.067 --> 00:01:53.611
Glucose and oxygen.

00:01:54.109 --> 00:01:56.444
Light and chlorophyll go above the arrow.

00:01:57.237 --> 00:01:57.657
Good.

00:01:58.115 --> 00:02:01.177
Light is an energy input,
not a chemical substance.

00:02:01.611 --> 00:02:04.632
Chlorophyll is the light-absorbing
pigment, not something you

00:02:04.632 --> 00:02:06.181
use up as a raw material.

00:02:06.622 --> 00:02:08.323
Now look at the symbol equation.

00:02:09.214 --> 00:02:15.131
Six carbon dioxide plus six water makes
one glucose plus six oxygen molecules.

00:02:15.885 --> 00:02:17.186
Read the formula cards.

00:02:17.422 --> 00:02:26.634
6CO2 + 6H2O produces C6H12O6 + 6O2.

00:02:26.968 --> 00:02:29.061
Those big sixes count molecules.

00:02:29.422 --> 00:02:32.349
The small numbers count
atoms within each molecule.

00:02:33.070 --> 00:02:34.730
Could I erase the big sixes?

00:02:35.140 --> 00:02:36.587
It would look much tidier.

00:02:37.418 --> 00:02:39.262
Tidier but chemically wrong.

00:02:39.980 --> 00:02:42.279
Glucose contains six carbon atoms.

00:02:42.519 --> 00:02:45.423
One carbon dioxide
molecule supplies only one.

00:02:45.803 --> 00:02:50.173
Count both sides before you hand
it in: six carbons, 12 hydrogens,

00:02:50.312 --> 00:02:52.442
and 18 oxygens on each side.

00:02:53.216 --> 00:02:54.360
18 oxygens?

00:02:54.829 --> 00:02:56.899
I counted 12 in the oxygen gas.

00:02:57.691 --> 00:03:03.049
Add the six oxygen atoms
inside glucose, 12 + 6 = 18.

00:03:03.381 --> 00:03:05.350
No atoms disappear behind the arrow.

00:03:05.692 --> 00:03:08.355
The balanced equation
conserves each kind of atom.

00:03:09.135 --> 00:03:12.673
Atom accountant, another
glamorous science career.

00:03:13.424 --> 00:03:18.256
A final twist, the oxygen gas released
during photosynthesis comes from water.

00:03:18.872 --> 00:03:22.081
Carbon dioxide supplies the
carbon used to build glucose.

00:03:22.583 --> 00:03:26.966
The summary equation tells us the
totals, not every tiny reaction step

00:03:27.367 --> 00:03:29.034
Here is a leaf cross-section model.

00:03:29.488 --> 00:03:32.646
What is the difference between
chlorophyll and a chloroplast?

00:03:33.431 --> 00:03:37.514
Chlorophyll is the little green
room, and chloroplast is the paint?

00:03:38.243 --> 00:03:38.848
Swap them.

00:03:39.669 --> 00:03:42.379
A chloroplast is a structure
inside a plant cell.

00:03:42.848 --> 00:03:45.703
Chlorophyll is the pigment
inside it that absorbs light.

00:03:46.234 --> 00:03:49.003
Structure and substance are
different words for a reason.

00:03:49.834 --> 00:03:51.223
Chloroplast is the room.

00:03:51.618 --> 00:03:53.644
Chlorophyll catches the light inside it.

00:03:54.045 --> 00:03:54.582
Got it.

00:03:55.356 --> 00:03:58.234
Chlorophyll absorbs red
and blue light strongly.

00:03:58.569 --> 00:04:03.108
More green light is reflected or passes
through, which helps leaves look green.

00:04:03.394 --> 00:04:06.702
That does not mean a whole leaf
uses absolutely no green light.

00:04:07.489 --> 00:04:11.988
So green leaves aren't proof that green
is their favorite light to absorb?

00:04:12.768 --> 00:04:13.208
Right.

00:04:13.511 --> 00:04:17.091
A leaf is broad to intercept
light and thin, so gases have

00:04:17.093 --> 00:04:18.585
a short diffusion distance.

00:04:19.179 --> 00:04:22.966
Its transparent upper surface lets
light reach the palisade cells,

00:04:23.180 --> 00:04:24.928
which are packed with chloroplasts.

00:04:25.749 --> 00:04:29.325
Like putting the solar panels
upstairs instead of in the basement.

00:04:30.061 --> 00:04:30.849
Exactly.

00:04:31.262 --> 00:04:34.918
Below them, spongy mesophyll cells
have air spaces between them.

00:04:35.259 --> 00:04:39.347
Carbon dioxide diffuses through these
spaces to photosynthesizing cells.

00:04:39.713 --> 00:04:40.080
Diffusion is net movement from
higher to lower concentration.
